\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar hits 5-month high vs yen, BOJ suspected.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By John Parry  \par \uc2 721 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 18:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, March 8 (Reuters) - The dollar hit a five-month high against the yen on Monday and steadied against the euro, supported by suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the greenback from sliding after Friday's dismal U.S. jobs data.  \par \par \uc2 Persistent softness in the U.S. labor market appears to offer little prospect of an increase in official U.S. interest rates any time soon, which will likely hurt the dollar against \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  which offer higher yields to investors.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said there was demand for dollars against yen from Japanese and U.S. commercial banks and cited speculation the Bank of Japan may have been among bidders around 112.0 yen.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan, which acts on behalf of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is aiming to weaken the yen ahead of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fiscal year close at the end of March as Japanese companies repatriate earnings from abroad. A weaker yen helps boost corporate results.  \par \par \uc2 "There is solid interest from Tokyo money center banks," said Craig Russell, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer with Alaron \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Chicago, adding that the dollar "has a bid tone to it" against the yen.  \par \par \uc2 Should the dollar push above Monday's five-month highs, one of the next key areas would be 112.70 yen, a decisive break above which could pave the way for a dollar climb to about 113.10 yen, he said.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier in Europe, the dollar rose as high as 112.32 yen, surpassing Friday's peak by a whisker to notch its highest level since late September.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers estimated Japan spent almost 1 trillion yen on Friday to support the dollar and suspected Japanese authorities were still conducting covert yen-selling activity on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 "There is no sign the BoJ is ready to step back from its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Mansoor Mohi-uddin, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS Warburg.  \par \par \uc2 Around noon in New York, the euro traded at $1.2367, steady from the previous New York close and a good distance from the euro's three-month low last Wednesday of $1.2056. On Friday, the disappointing U.S. jobs report hurt the dollar and pushed the euro up as high as $1.2432.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the dollar was trading at 112.10 yen, nearly flat on the day.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was near a recent eight-month high versus the yen, trading at 138.64.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling traded little changed at $1.8470.  \par \par \uc2 "Ultimately, the activities from Japan are helping the dollar in general," said Derek Halpenny, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Bank of Tokyo Mitsubishi in London.  \par \par \uc2 "There is still a belief in the market that the BoJ are here or just below here. They have clearly set out on a very determined effort to drive the yen weaker."  \par \par \uc2 But against most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  the dollar's underlying sentiment was bearish, after Friday's news that the U.S. economy created far fewer jobs than expected in February convinced markets that yield-boosting U.S. interest rate hikes remained a distant prospect.  \par \par \uc2 For the euro, "the $1.2330 level is key on the downside. Consolidation below that would indicate the strengthening U.S. dollar (move) is still intact, but above that (level, for the euro) we are still not so convinced," said Susan Stearns, vice president of institutional \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales with Bank of Montreal in New York.  \par \par \uc2 "At this juncture the euro bulls are still quite eager to consider ... that the trend for a higher euro remains intact," after Friday's "ugly" reversal lower for the dollar, Stearns added.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said factors that have punished the dollar in recent months - hefty U.S. budget and trade deficits, ultra-low interest rates and feeble job creation - still shadow the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Little in the way of major economic data releases were due on Monday, and European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet said central bankers from the Group of 10 nations, meeting in Basel, did not discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.  \par \par \uc2 But traders remain nervous about what Trichet might say.  \par \par \uc2 His comments about "brutal" \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves when the euro scaled record highs in January contributed to keeping the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from breaking above the $1.30 level. (Additional reporting by Justyna Pawlak and Christina Fincher in London).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040308e038002va\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
