\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar hits five-month high vs yen, BoJ suspected.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Justyna Pawlak  \par \uc2 636 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 14:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, March 8 (Reuters) - The dollar hit a five-month high against the yen on Monday and steadied against the euro with the help of suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the greenback from sliding after Friday's dismal U.S. jobs data.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said bearish dollar sentiment dominated after Friday's news that the U.S. economy created far fewer jobs than expected in February convinced markets that yield-boosting U.S. interest rate hikes remained a distant prospect.  \par \par \uc2 But suspected selling of yen for dollars by the Bank of Japan (BoJ) kept a floor under the greenback across a range of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after its 2-1/2 cent tumble versus the euro on Friday took it down nearly four cents from last week's peaks versus the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "Ultimately, the activities from Japan are helping the dollar in general," said Derek Halpenny, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Bank of Tokyo Mitsubishi in London.  \par \par \uc2 "There is still a belief in the market that the BoJ are here or just below here. They have clearly set out on a very determined effort to drive the yen weaker.  \par \par \uc2 "If bids weren't there at 111.00 after the payrolls, dollar/yen would have tumbled. That would have just accelerated the move of dollar selling elsewhere," he said.  \par \par \uc2 At 1300 GMT, the dollar traded at $1.2362 to the euro, steady from the previous New York close and a good distance from Wednesday's three-month high of $1.2056.  \par \par \uc2 On Friday, the disappointing jobs report pushed it down to as low as $1.2432 per euro from session highs around $1.2173.  \par \par \uc2 BOJ HAND SUSPECTED  \par \par \uc2 The dollar hit its highest level since late September against the yen at 112.32 yen.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was also near a recent eight month high versus the yen, trading at 138.69.  \par \par \uc2 Japan has spent 10 trillion yen ($89.15 billion) in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets so far this year, compared with 20 trillion yen for all of last year, a record in itself, in a bid to protect the country's export competitiveness.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier on Monday, BoJ Governor Toshihiko Fukui said that Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan has not criticised \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the rapid appreciation of the yen against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "Fukui's comment that Greenspan wasn't critical of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy suggests the BoJ will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Mansoor Mohi-uddin, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS in London.  \par \par \uc2 "This is keeping the yen weak against both the dollar and the euro...The market suspects Japan is keen to help exporters dress up their balance sheets ahead of the end-March fiscal year-end."  \par \par \uc2 INVESTORS HESITATE  \par \par \uc2 The dollar's Friday tumble put a brake on its sharp rise from the mid-February record low against the euro of $1.2927 to $1.2056 last week, leaving investors wondering whether the dollar had more room to gain or whether it would return to a downtrend now.  \par \par \uc2 "Euro/dollar is difficult now. It may take a few more weeks before the market becomes more confident to push the pair higher, in the short term there is a lot of noise," said Kamal Sharma, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Dresdner Kleinwort Wasserstein.  \par \par \uc2 Little in the way of major economic data releases is due on Monday and European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet said central bankers from the Group of 10 nations, meeting in Basel, did not discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.  \par \par \uc2 But Trichet later takes part in the Eurogroup meeting of euro zone finance ministers and markets are nervous about what he might say.  \par \par \uc2 His comments about "brutal" \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves when the euro scaled record highs in January kept the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from breaking $1.30.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040308e0380027h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
