\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar fall stops after Friday slide, eyes on BoJ.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Justyna Pawlak  \par \uc2 585 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 12:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, March 8 (Reuters) - The dollar was close to five-month highs against the yen on Monday and steadied against the euro with the help of suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the greenback from sliding after Friday's dismal U.S. jobs data.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said bearish dollar sentiment dominated after Friday's news that the U.S. economy created far fewer jobs than expected in February convinced markets that yield-boosting U.S. interest rate hikes remained a distant prospect.  \par \par \uc2 But suspected yen-selling by the Bank of Japan (BoJ) kept a floor under the greenback across a range of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after its 2-1/2 cent tumble versus the euro on Friday took it down nearly four cents from last week's peaks versus the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "Ultimately, the activities from Japan are helping the dollar in general," said Derek Halpenny, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Bank of Tokyo Mitsubishi in London.  \par \par \uc2 "There is still a belief in the market that the BoJ are here or just below here. They have clearly set out on a very determined effort to drive the yen weaker.  \par \par \uc2 "If bids weren't there at 111.00 after the payrolls, dollar/yen would have tumbled. That would have just accelerated the move of dollar selling elsewhere," he said.  \par \par \uc2 At 1100 GMT, the dollar traded at $1.2374, steady from the previous New York close and a good distance from Wednesday's three-month high of $1.2056.  \par \par \uc2 It was also unchanged on the day at 112.04 yen after rising near Friday's five-month highs around 112.30, which dealers also suspected came with the help of Japanese authorities.  \par \par \uc2 Japan has spent 10 trillion yen ($89.15 billion) to buy dollars against yen so far this year, compared with 20 trillion yen for all of last year, a record in itself, in a bid to protect the country's export competitiveness.  \par \par \uc2 The country's Vice Finance Minister Masakazu Hayashi reiterated on Monday that Japan's stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy remained unchanged.  \par \par \uc2 WHERE NOW?  \par \par \uc2 The dollar's Friday tumble put a brake on its sharp rise from the mid-February record low against the euro of $1.2927 to $1.2056 last week, leaving investors wondering whether the dollar had more room to gain or whether it would return to a downtrend now.  \par \par \uc2 Little in the way of major economic data releases is due on Monday, but markets traded nervously ahead of the 1130 GMT news conference of central bankers from the Group of 10 (G10) nations, during the bi-monthly Bank of International Settlements meeting in Switzerland.  \par \par \uc2 Markets felt European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet's comments about "brutal" \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves when the euro scaled record highs in January kept the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from breaking $1.30.  \par \par \uc2 Trichet also takes part in the Eurogroup meeting of euro zone finance ministers, which starts on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Investors will be eager to see if any more warnings come from Monday's events.  \par \par \uc2 "If you want to go long euro/dollar and you didn't do it straight after Friday's U.S. jobs data and get the first upmove, then you probably don't want to do it ahead of these policy maker events," said Aziz McMahon, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN AMRO in London.  \par \par \uc2 "Euro/dollar may tread water today then head higher over the remainder of the week once policy maker events are out of the way."   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040308e038001rz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
