\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Fukui-Fed not criticising  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2 .   \b0\par\par\uc2 223 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 10:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BASEL, Switzerland, March 8 (Reuters) - Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Toshihiko Fukui said on Monday that Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan has not criticised \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the rapid appreciation of the yen against the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Fukui, speaking to reporters on the sidelines of the Group of 10 meeting of central bankers from top industrialised and emerging markets, also repeated that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates would move in line with fundamentals.   \par \par \uc2 "Greenspan is not talking critically," of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, Fukui said.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets regularly because the Japanese government wants to prevent the yen from rising too fast and thus help export competitiveness as its economy recovers from a decade-long slump.   \par \par \uc2 The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said that Asian efforts to stabilise their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are putting upward pressure on the euro, and the Group of Seven in its recent financial policy statements has called for Asian regions to pursue flexible exchange rates.   \par \par \uc2 With the Japanese economy now perking up, long-term interest rates are starting to rise. Asked about this, Fukui expressed no concern. "They are relatively calm," he said.   \par \par \uc2 But he did say that higher commodity prices were affecting corporations. Asked if this posed a risk to Japanese firms, Fukui said "Yes."    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040308e038001i7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
