\par\par \b \uc2 Japan MOF buys back some foreign bonds from BOJ.  \b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 07:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, March 8 (Reuters) - Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) likely bought back some of the foreign bonds it sold to the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) to raise funds for yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 The BOJ data showed the outstanding amount of foreign securities purchased from the MOF's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  special account totaled 6.1489 trillion yen ($54.81 billion).  \par \par \uc2 Separate data previously showed the government had sold 10 trillion yen - the total allowable under a framework agreed in December - in foreign bonds held as official reserves to the BOJ to avoid a funding crunch in its efforts to stem the yen's rise.  \par \par \uc2 The buyback gives the MOF leeway to again sell foreign bonds to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the end of March if necessary.  \par \par \uc2 The MOF was likely able to buy back some of the bonds as the government expanded the limit of allowable debt issuance to raise funds for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The ministry normally borrows yen by selling financing bills (FBs) to pay for its dollar-buying in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 The limit on issuing FBs was raised to 100 trillion yen from 79 trillion yen in a supplementary budget for the year ending in March.  \par \par \uc2 It is widely believed that the ministry had hit the FB limit imposed by parliament and was forced to take stopgap measures, including selling foreign bondholdings to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  under the repurchase agreement.  \par \par \uc2 The government sold a record 20 trillion yen in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market last year, and over 10 trillion yen in the first two months of this year.  \par \par \uc2 The government is seeking to raise the borrowing limit to 140 trillion yen in the fiscal year starting in April. ($1=112.16 yen).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040308e0380011j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
