\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar surges vs yen on suspected  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Daniel Bases   \par \uc2 659 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 23:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, March 5 (Reuters) - The dollar's surge against the yen on Friday despite a grim February jobs report that sent it careening lower against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  indicates massive yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Tokyo, traders and analysts said.   \par \par \uc2 While it is impossible to know exactly how much Japan spent to prop up the dollar against the yen, the dollar's startlingly strong move up versus the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a day it fell sharply elsewhere indicates the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was huge.   \par \par \uc2 "The latest surge in dollar/yen appears to be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 -driven. Frankly it is impossible to see fundamental reasons that justify this as Japanese economic data continue to improve and foreign buying of Japanese assets is increasing," said Rebecca Patterson, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at J.P. Morgan Chase in New York.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar rose to a five-month high near 112.29 yen  according to\par Reuters data, a gain of more than 1 percent from Thursday's New York\par close. The euro climbed to an eight-month high of 138.96 yen          ,\par up 2.5 percent on the day.\par In contrast the greenback fell more than 1.25 percent against the euro\par , Swiss franc , sterling  and Australian dollar        after the U.S.\par Labor Department reported a paltry 21,000 jobs added in February.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Economists had forecast creation of 125,000 jobs.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While the market will have to wait for official March \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  figures from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  speculation was rife as to the size of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Directly after the jobs report, the dollar fell across the board except against the yen. The dollar held nearly unchanged for more than two hours around 111.00 yen after the data.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We were guessing earlier that there was around $5 billion worth of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  around the 111 yen level," said one senior trader at a Japanese bank in New York.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Below 111 (yen), there were huge stop-losses in the billions (of dollars). The market got short dollars which meant the failure to break 111 yen finally prompted some stop-loss dollar buying on the way up," the trader said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rumors about the size and scope of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  circulated in the market. One New York trader, who requested anonymity, thought the size could have been much larger.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "They (Japanese banks) came in again at the 112.15 yen area this afternoon. Now people are talking of 20 yards ($20 billion) done by the BOJ. From the 111 yen to 111.50 yen area, the talk was 10 yards. Seems to have doubled that since."   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While the size on a given day would be considered huge, it is not beyond possibility.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MOF data on Friday showed Japan's external reserves bulging to $776.86 billion at the end of February, a record high for the sixth straight month and up $35.61 billion from the end of January.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The figures were in line with the MOF's announcement a week earlier that its market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last month had totaled 3.34 trillion yen ($30.07 billion). That brought the total for the first two months of this year above 10 trillion yen - already half of last year's record 20 trillion yen.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Assuming the huge \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , conducted by the BOJ on behalf of the MOF, occurred on Friday, it comes just days after Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan said the consequences of continued large-scale \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for an improving economy would no longer meet \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's monetary policy needs.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Greenspan already commented on it this week and it is only a matter of time before (U.S.) Treasury does as well. The U.S. is trying to create jobs and it is only a matter of time before U.S. politicians protest at what they see as a threat to our ability to create jobs," said J.P. Morgan Chase's Patterson. (Additional reporting by Gertrude Chavez in New York).    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040305e035003h3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
