\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar keeps firm tone in wait for U.S. jobs data.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Burton Frierson  \par \uc2 602 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 13:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, March 5 (Reuters) - The dollar extended recent gains to four-month highs on the yen and held fairly steady versus the euro on Friday on expectations the United States would report jobs data later that could hasten U.S. interest rate hikes.  \par \par \uc2 Bets the U.S. saw its fastest jobs growth in more than three years last month boosted the dollar this week to 2004 peaks versus the yen and the euro. Investors are now focused on whether the 125,000 new jobs analysts have forecast for the 1330 GMT report will materialise. The greenback received help climbing above 111.40 yen, its highest since November 3, from speculation \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has continued \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen after stopping its rise at 3-1/2 year highs versus the dollar set last month.  \par \par \uc2 "It's all about the payroll result. That's absolutely pivotal to whether or not this bear market rally in the dollar can continue and thus develop the potential to turn into something more serious," said Steven Pearson, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Halifax Bank of Scotland Treasury Services.  \par \par \uc2 "If we do get a decent payroll report that will bring forward expectations of the first rate hike from the U.S. Federal Reserve."  \par \par \uc2 By 1240 GMT the dollar remained little changed on the day at $1.2190 per euro.  \par \par \uc2 After the dollar rallied nearly five cents earlier this week to peak at $1.2056, slight support for the euro emerged on Thursday from the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which held rates steady at two percent and gave no sign an interest rate cut was near.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar retreated a little by European midsession to 111.21 yen, a touch firmer versus its previous New York close, and markets remained focused on possible Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "No one is ready to put on short dollar/yen positions," said Niels Christensen, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Societe Generale in Paris.  \par \par \uc2 WEAK SPOT  \par \par \uc2 The labour market has been the weak spot in the U.S. economic recovery and the market is looking for signs of stronger growth in payrolls to prompt the U.S. Federal Reserve to raise interest rates and make dollar returns more attractive.  \par \par \uc2 Economic derivatives offered by Deutsche Bank and Goldman Sachs showed markets betting on Friday for February jobs growth of around 137,000. Markets had been going for about 145,000 on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Job growth in January came in at 112,000.  \par \par \uc2 "I'm pretty confident the market is quite uncertain about the outcome because recent history has displayed a tendency for the payrolls to disappoint relative to the consensus," said Pearson at HBOS.  \par \par \uc2 "I don't think the market is going to believe anything with conviction until we see the number in black and white."  \par \par \uc2 Also in focus is a news conference with ECB President Jean-Claude Trichet and Bank of France Governor Christian Noyer at 1430 GMT and an appearance by U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow at 1630 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 On Thursday, Trichet said rates were appropriate and the economic risks balanced - ECB code for unchanged monetary policy in the months ahead.  \par \par \uc2 This disappointed those in the markets who thought the recent high levels of the euro - which hit a record peak of $1.2927 in February - might lead the ECB to ease rates to help euro zone exporters.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, dealers suspected the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  intermittently in dollar/yen from around 110.50 on Thursday, raising speculating Japan is determined to prevent the dollar's recovery from faltering.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040305e0350021p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
