\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar holds firm in Europe, US jobs data awaited.  \b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 09:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 5 (Reuters) - The dollar rose to a four-month high on the yen but sat tight against the euro ahead of a key U.S. jobs report on Friday which was expected to be a major determinant as to whether its bull run continues.   \par \par \uc2  After making a four cent dash higher against the euro this week, the dollar has backed off a three-month peak and paused at $1.2200  in the wait for the jobs numbers.   \par \par \uc2  The labour market is the weak spot in the U.S. economic recovery and the market is looking for signs of stronger growth in payrolls to prompt the U.S. Federal Reserve to raise interest rates and make dollar returns more attractive.   \par \par \uc2  Forecasts are for a rise in payrolls of 125,000 in February compared with 112,000 in January. The unemployment rate is expected to remain steady at 5.6 percent.   \par \par \uc2  Also in focus is a news conference with European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet and Bank of France governor Christian Noyer at 1430 GMT and an appearance by U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow at 1630.   \par \par \uc2  The dollar climbed to 111.43 yen  in Asian trading but had trimmed gainst to stand at 111.12 by 0755 GMT.   \par \par \uc2  Dealers suspected the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen for dollars intermittently from around 110.50, helping the greenback to the four-month high.   \par \par \uc2  Japan's lower house of parliament passed the state budget for the year starting in April, giving the government the means to continue its huge \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at preventing the yen from strengthening and jeopardising export-led recovery.   \par \par \uc2  Other data include euro zone retail sales for January at 1000 GMT.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040305e0350014j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
