/ECONOMY\par     TOKYO - The dollar extends its month-long rally, hitting a\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par four-month high versus the yen on expectations of strong U.S.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par jobs data later in the day and speculation that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par continue to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stop the recovery from faltering.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MARKETS-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (UPDATE 3), expect by 0700, by Kazunori Takada,\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 600 words)\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TOKYO - Japan's foreign reserves hit a new high of $776.9\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion in February, swollen by the dollars it has amassed as a\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par result of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to a level that now\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exceeds its national budget (ECONOMY-JAPAN-RESERVES (UPDATE 2),\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par moved at 0332, by Hideyuki Sano, 650 words)\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SINGAPORE - Dollar rises to four-month highs against the\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yen, as optimism grows ahead of U.S. jobs data, helping boost\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japanese exporters while other Asian share markets struggle in\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par choppy trade (MARKETS-GLOBAL (WRAPUP 2), expect by 0700, by\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Brian Hansford, 700 words)\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BEIJING - Chinese Premier Wen Jiabao stresses need to rein\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in economy after years of breakneck growth and throw a lifeline\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to hundreds of millions in the poor countryside\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (CHINA-PARLIAMENT (WRAPUP 5) expect by 0800, picture, about 600\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     See also: CHINA-PARLIAMENT-ISSUES (FACTBOX), moved at 0133,\par 800 words)\par     SEOUL - South Korean wholesale prices grew at their fastest\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rate in more than five years in February, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par shows, underlining concerns over the impact of surging raw\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par material prices on a fragile economic recovery.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (ECONOMY-KOREA-PPI (UPDATE 2), expect by 0700, by Oh Jung-hwa\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and Yoo Choonsik, 600 words)\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI - From dusty Shandong province to the hushed\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par corridors of power in Beijing, Zhang Enzhao has quietly risen\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the ranks to head up China Construction Bank, the mainland's\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par healthiest state lender (FINANCIAL-CHINA-ZHANG (NEWSMAKER), by\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Ben Blanchard, expect by 0900, 750 words)\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TOKYO - Iraqi Communications Minister Haidar al-Ebadi\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expects to receive $100 million to help reconstruct his\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par country's telecommunications network out of the $1.5 billion\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japan has pledged to Iraq this year (IRAQ-JAPAN-TELECOMS\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (INTERVIEW), moving shortly, by Yukari Iwatani Kane, 550 words)\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TOKYO - Japanese and Mexican trade officials have stepped\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par up their push for an elusive free trade agreement that could\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par have implications for Tokyo's efforts to catch up with China in\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the race to forge similar deals in Asia (TRADE-JAPAN-MEXICO,\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par moved at 0137, by Masayuki Kitano, 600 words)\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TOKYO - Pom-pom waving cheerleaders, chants drawn from\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ancient warrior purification rituals, drummers, a brass band\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and ear-splitting rock music: all part of the mix at a Tokyo\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par jobs fair, getting students psyched up for the coming challenge\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in one of the toughest years for youth employment in Japan.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (LIFE-JAPAN-YOUTHEMPLOYMENT (PICTURE), expect by 0600, by\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Jonathan Standing, 600 words)\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SINGAPORE - The queue of trucks snaking from Yantian\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par container terminal in China's boom town of Shenzhen is growing\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par so long that port director Kenneth Tse installed remote TV\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par cameras to keep sight of the end, as truckers vie for a piece\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of China's booming econmy (TRANSPORT-ASIA-FREIGHT,(ANALYSIS),\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - - - -\par     ENERGY\par     SINGAPORE/SEOUL - A big recovery in the long-stagnant Asian\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par oil refining profit margins - driven by demand from China and\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japan - has fuelled a bull-run in shares of the region's\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par refineries (ENERGY-ASIA-REFINERY-SHARES (ANALYSIS), expect by\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0730, by Charlie Zhu and Park Sung-woo, about 850 words)\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SEE ALSO: ENERGY-ASIA-REFINERIES (TABLE)\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ENERGY-ASIA-REFINERY-SHARES (TABLE).\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 