\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar Tumbles Against European Rivals on Jobs Data  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Tom Barkley  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 405 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 22:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK -- The dollar fell sharply against most other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a disappointing U.S. employment report Friday, but hit a five-month high against the yen on apparent heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities.  \par \par \uc2 After much-awaited February payrolls data showed only 21,000 new nonfarm jobs were created in February, the dollar tumbled over two cents against the euro to $1.2437 and nearly three cents against the pound to $1.8505 before recouping some losses.  \par \par \uc2 However, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was able to advance against the yen on what on what was widely suspected to be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , say traders. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was estimated by some to have bought as much as $20 billion in an effort that eventually drove the dollar up over a yen to 112.37 yen, a level not seen since late September.  \par \par \uc2 The BOJ isn't expected to take its foot off the pedal ahead of end of the current fiscal year on March 31. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought a record amount of dollars in 2003 and so far this year to keep the yen from appreciating too far and jeopardizing the country's export-led recovery.  \par \par \uc2 Some market participants believe it may try to target 115 yen in a bid to help Japanese exporters and other companies who need to repatriate yen.  \par \par \uc2 Friday afternoon, the dollar was trading at 112.04 yen, up from 111.08 yen late Thursday. The euro was higher at $1.2364 from $1.2190. Sterling rose to $1.8456 from $1.8230.  \par \par \uc2 Except against the yen, any continuation of the dollar's corrective recovery is now in serious jeopardy, with hopes dashed of any shift in the outlook for interest rates in the near term.  \par \par \uc2 Coupled with the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision Thursday not to counter euro strength by signaling a possible rate cut, the payrolls report "was a double whammy for the dollar that should remain the dominant force in the market at least for the first part of the week," said Sean Callow, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at IDEAglobal, a New York-based financial-market research firm.  \par \par \uc2 -By Tom Barkley; Dow Jones Newswires; 201-938-4385; tom.barkley@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (Jamie McGeever contributed to this story.) [ 03-05-04 1648ET ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020040305e03500034\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
