\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  VIEW: Welcome To The Yen Free Float, Japan Style  \b0\par\par\uc2 1,048 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 23:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Grainne McCarthy and Jamie McGeever \par    A DOW JONES NEWSWIRES COLUMN \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The Martha Stewart guilty verdict may have been grabbing the headlines Friday, but another phenomenal story was also unfolding: massive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 The fact that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps into \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets regularly is no surprise. It buys dollars for yen in a bid to limit the fallout on its export-led economy from a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and reinvests those dollars in U.S. markets, typically in government bonds.  \par \par \uc2 But Japan's chutzpah in throwing billions of dollars into \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on a day that the U.S. government reported much weaker than expected jobs growth has surprised even the most seasoned \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market veterans.  \par \par \uc2 Prompting allegations that Japan is effectively trying to run a quasi-managed exchange rate, the consistent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , estimated at a staggering amount of up to $20 billion, pushed the dollar up over a yen to Y112.37, a level not seen since late September, even as the greenback was plunging against the euro and other counterparts.  \par \par \uc2 Just to put that in perspective, Japan bought a record monthly amount of about $67 billion in January; many observers suspect Friday's tally will prove to be a record outlay for one day.  \par \par \uc2 A dealer at a Japanese bank in New York said Japan's monetary authorities were aware of the huge stop-loss sell orders below Y111.00 that, if triggered could have sent the dollar plunging as low as Y109.00. "That's why it was necessary for the Bank of Japan to support Y111.00," he said. The BOJ acts in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on behalf of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Holding Y111.00 took out many speculators who were long of yen, who were then forced to go long of dollars. Continued \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  then forced dealers to increase their long dollar positions, which added to the greenback's upside momentum.  \par \par \uc2 Official bids, which traders say were ratcheted up from Y111.00 through several levels all the way up to Y112.15, were up to five times the size of normal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels. Indeed, on Friday, the BOJ was reported to be soaking up offers at up to $1 billion at a time, as opposed to around $200 million usually. Before the break above options-related resistance at Y111.50, one BOJ agent bank alone was said to have bought over $3 billion.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's onslaught on its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sent the yen reeling across the board. The pound and Australian dollar both hit fresh five-and-a-half-year-highs of Y207.35 and Y85.27, respectively, and the euro reached a new eight-month zenith of Y139.00.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par      Bold Swim Against The Tide \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For a market accustomed to the overbearing presence of the Bank of Japan, the bold swim against the weak dollar tide on Friday was remarkable and prompted a wave of speculation as to whether this represents a significant shift in strategy.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Typically the amounts apparently done (Friday) have only been used in the past when defending key levels," said Alan Ruskin, research director at 4Cast financial consultancy in New York. "So what's going on?"  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He ticked off some of what he termed "the least worst" conspiracy theories circulating in the market to answer that question, including the following:  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -That the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  wants an even higher dollar rate against the yen at the end of the March 31 fiscal year than previously thought. For what it is worth, last year the rate was Y118. Japanese corporations traditionally repatriate some of their assets held abroad to strengthen their balance sheets before books are closed at the fiscal yearend.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  wants to build a firebreak, such that if there are events that will prompt a slide in the dollar against the yen they have a large buffer above Y105 before they have to deal with it. Such events include general dollar weakness or a revaluation of the Chinese yuan, which currently trades in a tightly-controlled band against the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Japan's monetary authorities want to come off as unpredictable, so they are not perceived as only \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in a defensive manner to hold levels. According to that theory, unpredictability will help the efficacy of future \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Now that they are finally getting some bang for their buck, they may as well get some bang for their buck.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -They knew that given the weak U.S. payrolls number, the dollar could have been trading at Y108 on Friday. Instead, they have achieved a major split between what could have been had they not been there and what happened. In addition they have changed market psychology.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 None of these factors are necessarily totally convincing in and of themselves. But as Ruskin points out, together they build a case to explain the Japanese government's actions.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The nerve of Japan's play seems even more remarkable given Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan's warning this week that Japan's "awesome" accumulation of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves could become "problematic" and unsustainable for the world's second largest economy.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It may also spark some criticism from the Bush Administration, which analysts believe has reluctantly turned a blind eye to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  over the past year as it often seemed aimed at just "smoothing" rather than really turning around the exchange rate.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 What's more, Japan's economy is growing again and the U.S. is happy with the stimulus that potentially provides to the global economy. Japan has also proved a remarkable force in keeping the consumer-driven U.S. economy ticking along, via its massive purchases of Treasurys that help to keep market-based interest rates low, something that's expected to be evident again at next week's five-year and 10-year Treasury auctions.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 That means Japan's yen "free float" with a twist could well continue.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Grainne McCarthy is Assistant Managing Editor for fixed income, macroeconomics and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news. Grainne was previously Indonesia bureau chief and also reported for Dow Jones Newswires in Belgium).  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Grainne McCarthy; Dow Jones Newswires; 201 938 2381; grainne.mccarthy@dowjones.com [ 03-05-04 1742ET ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020040305e03500055\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
