\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Euro Slips Against Dlr On Adjustments Pre-ECB  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Takashi Nakamichi  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 708 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 06:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The euro lost ground against the dollar in Asia Thursday as investors adjusted positions ahead of the much awaited monetary policy meeting of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  later in the global day.  \par \par \uc2 After the euro's upside proved firm around $1.22 in early Sydney trading, medium- and long-term investors in Asia unloaded some euro longs, traders said. The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell as low as $1.215 as it tripped sell orders on its way down, though it later regained some lost ground.  \par \par \uc2 The movements show market participants are still adjusting positions ahead of the ECB policy meeting in order to react quickly to any outcome, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Although most players expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to leave interest rates unchanged at the current 2%, the market is preparing to scrutinize comments from ECB chief Jean-Claude Trichet for any clues about a possible rate cut ahead.  \par \par \uc2 "If there are no hints or suggestions of a rate cut in Trichet's remarks today, it could lead to euro buybacks, given that speculation of an ECB rate cut was one reason for the euro's recent losses," a Japanese trader said.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  was again in the market defending the dollar above Y110 Thursday according to Tokyo traders, putting a firm floor under the greenback.  \par \par \uc2 Recent criticism of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  tactics from Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan appears not to have dented the MOF's resolve to defend the Y110 point, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y110.14, above Y110.05 late Wednesday in New York. The dollar was at Y110.20 late Wednesday in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.2169, lower than $1.2205 late Wednesday in New York. The euro was at $1.2190 in Tokyo Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y134.06, down from Y134.38 in New York late Wednesday. The euro was at Y134.35 in Tokyo late Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.8281, down from $1.8300 in New York and lower than $1.8340 in Tokyo Wednesday. [ 04-03-04 0526GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 "It's just impossible for the dollar to be holding above Y110 without \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Mitsuo Imaizumi, deputy general manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Daiwa Securities SMBC.  \par \par \uc2 The hand of MOF was evident Wednesday in New York when the dollar held above Y110 even as the euro surged 150 pips to $1.2205, Imaizumi said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar hit an intraday high of Y110.21 Thursday after a senior Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  official indicated Tokyo wants the U.S. unit to make further headway.  \par \par \uc2 "I think (the reduction of short-dollar positions) is continuing," Zembei Mizoguchi, vice minister for international affairs, told reporters. "Either way, we are watching the market closely."  \par \par \uc2 Although gains in the Nikkei 225 Stock Average around midday raised overseas demand for the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is suspected to have absorbed yen purchases by investors abroad, keeping the exchange rate steady, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 But the MOF may face more dollar-selling pressure if U.S. jobless claims data due at 1330 GMT today fail to meet analysts' expectations.  \par \par \uc2 "Ahead of U.S. February employment data Friday, the market is watching U.S. jobless claims as a key determinant of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  direction this week," said Tohru Sasaki, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at J.P. Morgan Chase Bank in Tokyo. "If claims turn out to be larger than expected, that may lead to dollar sales," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The median estimate of 11 economists surveyed by Dow Jones Newswires and CNBC is for claims to fall by 5,000 in the week ended Feb. 28 to 345,000.  \par \par \uc2 -By Takashi Nakamichi, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Alastair Gale  \par \par \uc2 The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \par \par \uc2 Subscribers can find this table:  \par \par \uc2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \par \par \uc2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \par \par \uc2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \par \par \uc2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX [ 04-03-04 0648GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1074  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040304e03400030\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
