\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  plays down Greenspan remarks on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Mari Terawaki  \par \uc2 522 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 09:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, March 3 (Reuters) - Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki on Wednesday played down U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan's remark that Japan's economic recovery may soon no longer justify its large-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hold down the yen.  \par \par \uc2 Even though the economy logged its strongest growth in 13 years in the final three quarters of last year, deflation remains a concern and Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy stance remained unchanged, Tanigaki told reporters.  \par \par \uc2 "The Bank of Japan is committed to its monetary easing as long as deflation persists, but its policy will be different, naturally, when deflation has been overcome," Tanigaki said.  \par \par \uc2 "Our policy (the Finance Ministry's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy) once deflation is overcome will also be different from that when deflation is still persisting."  \par \par \uc2 Asked about the prospects for deflation, which has stifled investment and spending in Japan for nearly half a decade, Tanigaki said: "We cannot yet be optimistic."  \par \par \uc2 Greenspan had said on Tuesday that Asian central banks' purchases of U.S. dollar assets resulting from their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been "extraordinary" and, in the case of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , "awesome".  \par \par \uc2 "The current performance of the Japanese economy suggests that we are getting closer to the point where continued \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the present scale will no longer meet the monetary policy needs of Japan," Greenspan told the Economic Club of New York.  \par \par \uc2 NOT US  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  data last Friday showed that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had topped 10 trillion yen ($91 billion) in the first two months of this year - already half of last year's 20 trillion yen, which was an annual record.  \par \par \uc2 As Japan's gross domestic product figures have shown growth picking up strongly over the last few quarters, Japanese officials have begun to cite deflation, rather than the impact on exports, in justifying their \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hold down the yen.  \par \par \uc2 A higher yen adds to the downward pressure on prices as it makes imports cheaper. Yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also has a monetary easing effect as it tends to bring more yen funds into the private-sector banking system.  \par \par \uc2 By last month, the yen had risen around 20 percent over the past two years to scale 3-= year highs around 105 to the dollar , but it has since pulled back about five percent to hit a four-month low of around 110.40 on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Chief Cabinet Secretary Yasuo Fukuda, the Japanese government's top spokesman, insisted that Greenspan was not criticising \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "We do not take it as criticism towards us," he told a news conference.  \par \par \uc2 "If there are rapid swings in the future as well, we will take appropriate measures as necessary," he added. Fukushiro Nukaga, the head of the ruling Liberal Democratic Party's policy research council, concurred.  \par \par \uc2 "I think the (Greenspan) comments were meant as a check, but at the same time there seemed to be a sense that Japan shouldn't be criticised too much," Nukaga told reporters.  \par \par \uc2 "Japan's economy is finally starting to improve. It's natural to seek stability in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040303e033001fh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
