he comparative period strengthens, and company's not being as aggressive on price as a year ago. \par  \par Versatel (39126.AE): 4Q/FY Earnings \par Consensus 4Q loss (DJ, 4 analysts): EUR8.6M (EUR282.3M loss) \par Consensus FY net loss : EUR37.5M (EUR694.4M loss) \par Consensus sales: EUR460M (EUR294.4M) \par Note:  A big chunk of 2002 losses due to huge write-off. 4Q EBITDA seen +83% at EUR23.9M from EUR13M.  While sales seen +55% due to expansion in Germany, and addition of high-speed internet customers. Analysts eye 2004 outlook, company remarks about future FCF development. \par  \par Sulzer (SUN.VX): FY Earnings \par Consensus net profit (DJ, 4 analysts): CHF32M (CHF83M) \par Consensus EBIT: CHF58M (CHF113M) \par Consensus sales: CHF1.87B (CHF1.91B) \par Note:   Earnings expected to have been hit by effects of Swiss franc vs dollar exchange rates. Eyes on pump division performance as it generates around 50% of group's revenues and announcement about new CEO search, as Fred Kindle will leave for ABB. \par  \par OTHER SCHEDULED EVENTS: \par  \par Gallaher Group (GLH): FY Earnings \par  \par KLM (KLM): Feb Traffic Numbers \par  \par Coface (12068.FR): FY Earnings \par  \par MOL (MOL.BU): In case of oversubscription, govt may close domestic public offer. \par  \par Glanbia (GLB.DB): FY Earnings \par  \par SHL (SHL.LN): FY Earnings \par  \par Groupe Alten (7194.FR): FY Earnings \par  \par Stilo International (STL.LN): FY Earnings \par  \par Umicore (UMI.BT): FY Earnings \par  \par Vallourec (12035.FR): FY Earnings \par  \par Quayle Munroe Holdings (QYM.LN): FY Earnings \par  \par Rexel (12595.FR): FY Earnings \par  \par Biotrace International (BIO.LN): FY Earnings \par  \par Devro (DVO.LN): FY Earnings \par  \par Flying Brands Ltd (FBDU.LN): FY Earnings \par  \par Econocom Group (ECONB.BT): FY Earnings \par  \par Lorien (LRG.LN): FY Earnings \par  \par Marlborough Stirling (MAS.LN): FY Earnings \par  \par Mucklow Group (MKLW.LN): 1H Earnings \par  \par NXT (NTX.LN)