\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Rises; Fed Japan Critique Shrugged Off  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Takashi Nakamichi  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 812 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 06:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar built on overnight gains to rise against both the yen and euro in Asia Wednesday, with traders shrugging off criticism from the Federal Reserve's chairman of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's massive yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign.  \par \par \uc2 Traders in Asia rushed to liquidate long-euro positions against the dollar after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's tumble below key support at $1.235 overnight, players said.  \par \par \uc2 And Fed boss Alan Greenspan's criticism Tuesday of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy didn't lead to yen buying in Asian hours, due to speculation that whatever Greenspan said, Tokyo will likely continue selling the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market.  \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't stop \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Mitsuo Imaizumi, deputy general manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Daiwa Securities SMBC Co. "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has the U.S.'s permission to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  - even before the Group of Seven meeting in Florida - because it's been helping stabilize long-term interest rates in the U.S."  \par \par \uc2 Such sentiment helped keep the dollar above the psychologically important Y110.00-level throughout Asian trading hours.  \par \par \uc2 Speculation that Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  is defending Y110.00, sparked by bids placed around that level by Japanese banks often associated with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , also supported the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the yen.  \par \par \uc2 Greenspan said Tuesday at a luncheon that Japan's efforts to curb rises in the yen have led to "awesome" stock of dollar reserves that could soon become "problematic" for the Japanese economy.  \par \par \uc2 "I don't think the market dismissed Greenspan's remarks outright," said Tatsuro Karitani, vice president of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Mizuho Corporate Bank. "But at a time the market is intent on buying back dollars, they took a back seat."  \par \par \uc2 At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y110.20, above Y110.10 late Tuesday in New York. The dollar was at Y109.35 late Tuesday in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.2174, lower than $1.2210 late Tuesday in New York. The euro was at $1.2400 in Tokyo Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y134.13, down from Y134.45 in New York late Tuesday. The euro was at Y135.60 in Tokyo late Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.8310, down from $1.8395 in New York and lower than $1.8640 in Tokyo Tuesday. [ 03-03-04 0532GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Analysts were divided on whether the dollar's recent rallies herald a long phase of strength or a short-term correction.  \par \par \uc2 The dominant idea is that the dollar weakness isn't over given continued terrorism concerns, low U.S. interest rates and the widening U.S. budget and current account deficits.  \par \par \uc2 The euro's dive against the dollar overnight was technically driven, spot traders said.  \par \par \uc2 But deep behind the move may be disappointment about the single unit's past failures to break above $1.3, growing complaints by European officials about the euro's strength, and talk about a possible rate cut by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Mizuho's Karitani said.  \par \par \uc2 Ryohei Muramatsu, manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Commerzbank in Tokyo, said the dollar's long-term outlook remains bearish against the yen.  \par \par \uc2 Given the steady pickup in Japan's economy and rising demand for Japanese stocks abroad, "the Bank of Japan's tankan survey (of corporate sentiment) in April will probably serve as a signal for a shift back to a yen-buying mood," Muramatsu said.  \par \par \uc2 Also, despite continued expansion in Japan's trade surplus, the trade-weighted rate of the yen is "widely undervalued" by historical standards, said Tohru Sasaki, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at J.P. Morgan Chase Bank in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 "Fundamentals and positioning are both indicating a dollar-bearish trend will resume soon," Sasaki said. U.S. job data Friday may "trigger the resumption of a dollar downtrend" if the figures fail to meet expectations, he said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar may get some support from John Kerry, who looks to have sealed the U.S. Democratic nomination after winning nine of ten states in the Super Tuesday primaries.  \par \par \uc2 On his Web site, Kerry criticized China and Japan, saying they have "purposely kept their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  undervalued relative to the U.S. dollar to promote exports."  \par \par \uc2 If he raises the topic during debates with President George W. Bush, the incumbent may have trouble defending Japan, Imaizumi said.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Takashi Nakamichi, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Alastair Gale  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The chart of late Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates that accompanied Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been replaced with an enhanced \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Subscribers can find this table:  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX [ 03-03-04 0730GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1074  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040303e033000f0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
