\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Govt Fukuda: Will  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  As Needed  \b0\par\par\uc2 294 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 03:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Nikkei/Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top government spokesman said Wednesday Tokyo's policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market remains in place after Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan said overnight Japan's yen-selling campaign is unsustainable.  \par \par \uc2 "There's no change to our stance of acting as needed" in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, Chief Cabinet Secretary Yasuo Fukuda told a regular news conference.  \par \par \uc2 Greenspan warned Tuesday that Japan's efforts to prevent its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from rising against the dollar have resulted in an "awesome" accumulation of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves that could soon become "problematic" for the world's second-largest economy.  \par \par \uc2 In prepared remarks to the Economic Club of New York, Greenspan said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's pace of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unsustainable. "It must be presumed that the rate of accumulation of dollar assets by the Japanese government will have to slow at some point and eventually cease," he said.  \par \par \uc2 "I don't consider (his remarks) as criticism" of Japan, Fukuda said.  \par \par \uc2 Greenspan's "reference to Japan was in the context of the U.S. and global economy. It didn't seem like he was blaming Japan," Fukuda added.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , worried that a stronger yen could derail the country's economic recovery by hurting exports, sold an unprecedented Y20.05 trillion last year in an effort to rein in the surging \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It has stepped up the pace of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year, selling Y10 trillion in January and February.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar traded above Y110 for the first time in four months in New York Tuesday with Japan's monetary authorities suspected of helping the dollar higher.  \par \par \uc2 At 0304 GMT, the U.S. unit was trading around Y110.18. [ 03-03-04 0307GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040303e033000c0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
