\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Up Vs Yen On Suspected MOF  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Takashi Nakamichi  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 1,445 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 06:49\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar rose slightly against the yen in Asia Tuesday amid rumors that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities covertly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese banks that often receive orders from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on behalf of the Finance Ministry, were spotted buying dollars for yen in early Asian trade, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The widely suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  absorbed dollar sales by Japanese exporters and overseas investors seeking to purchase Japanese stocks, helping the U.S. unit advance 15 sen to near Y109.11 around midday, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Tokyo players suspect Japan's MOF was trying to stem the yen's appreciation after the benchmark Nikkei 225 Stock Average surged to a 20-month high Monday, which raised demand for the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  abroad.  \par \par \uc2 After the dollar/yen has risen gradually for the past two weeks, the pair's short-term outlook has dimmed as a bout of buybacks by speculators appears over, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 "Why hasn't the Y110 level been broken yet? Exporters are selling, and more importantly, position adjustments have run their course, as shown by International Monetary Market data yesterday," said Takashi Toyahara, executive director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Nomura Securities Co.  \par \par \uc2 The Chicago Mercantile Exchange's IMM \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market data, a barometer for sentiment in the spot market, suggest speculators may have finished closing dollar-bearish positions and may no longer need to buy back dollars.  \par \par \uc2 But Tokyo players may remain wary of yen-selling against the dollar after the Japanese government sold more than Y10 trillion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in January and February to limit the yen's advance, said Naomi Fink, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at BNP Paribas in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese financial officials reminded the market Tuesday they won't let the dollar fall without a fight.  \par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said his ministry will act against speculative moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and said that the yen is still adjusting.  \par \par \uc2 At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y109.04, above Y108.95 late Monday in New York. The dollar was at Y109.25 late Monday in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.2434, lower than $1.2460 late Monday in New York. It was at $1.2530 in Tokyo Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y135.64, down from Y135.75 in New York late Monday. The euro was at 136.85 in Tokyo late Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.8665, down from $1.8700 in New York but higher than $1.8745 in Tokyo Monday. [ 02-03-04 0549GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 The euro fell as low as $1.2431 before noon in subdued trade as speculators chose to stay on the sidelines ahead of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy meeting and data Friday on the employment situation in the U.S., traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The implications of these events on interest rates will be a key factor for the short-term direction for U.S. and European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Tokyo players doubt the ECB will cut its benchmark interest rate from 2% Thursday, which may weaken the euro, as the euro zone economy continues to recover. But they'll be listening to any comments by ECB President Jean-Claude Trichet for clues about any possible rate hike ahead.  \par \par \uc2 Comments from various Federal Reserve officials over the past few weeks suggest they'll be holding interest rates at 45-year lows until the U.S. labor market and inflation pick up. As a result, players will be watching U.S. non-farm payrolls data due out Friday to assess when the Fed may tighten policy.  \par \par \uc2 "The euro may soar back near $1.30 if Trichet says he won't slash rates for a while and if data show the U.S. job market is unchanged or worsening," a Tokyo trader said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar has suffered over the past two years as a low-return \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  compared with the euro, the pound and the Australian dollar. But rate hikes by the Fed alone won't be enough to end the dollar's downtrend, BNP Paribas's Fink said.  \par \par \uc2 "A rate increase now wouldn't reduce U.S. current account deficits," Fink said. "It may rather hurt U.S. stocks by making it harder for corporations to finance (their \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ). It may also affect government and corporate bonds."  \par \par \uc2 Fink said by the end of March, the U.S. unit is likely to slip back near Y107, as the MOF will likely keep slowing the dollar's slide rather than actively pushing it higher.  \par \par \uc2 For now, though, options trade appears to suggest players expect the dollar and yen to hold steady until Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Some banks sold yen put/dollar call options allowing the buyers to purchase $60 million at a rate of Y109.60 when the contracts expire Friday, an options dealer said. As the expiration will come before the release of the closely watched U.S. employment data, "the sellers may not be expecting to see much movement in the spot until then," a Japanese options broker said.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Takashi Nakamichi, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by John Gibson, Kirsty Mackenzie and Hugh Lawson  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The chart of late Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates that accompanied Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been replaced with an enhanced \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Subscribers can find this table:  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX [ 02-03-04 0734GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro fell as low as $1.2431 before noon in subdued trade as speculators chose to stay on the sidelines ahead of the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's policy meeting and data Friday on the employment situation in the U.S., traders said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The implications of these events on interest rates will be a key factor for the short-term direction for U.S. and European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo players doubt the ECB will cut its benchmark interest rate from 2% Thursday, which may weaken the euro, as the euro zone economy continues to recover. But they'll be listening to any comments by ECB President Jean-Claude Trichet for clues about any possible rate hike ahead.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Comments from various Federal Reserve o