\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar extends rally ahead of US-Germany talks.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Natsuko Waki  \par \uc2 577 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Februar 2004\par 11:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Feb 27 (Reuters) - The dollar extended this week's rally to fresh one-month highs versus the euro on Friday as technically-driven buying accelerated ahead of German Chancellor Gerhard Schroeder's talks with U.S. President George W. Bush.  \par \par \uc2 A government source has said Schroeder will make the euro's strength against the dollar a main theme in his meeting with Bush.  \par \par \uc2 The euro has lost more than five cents since hitting a record high against the dollar only last week, with speculation that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might consider lowering interest rates if there is evidence that euro strength is putting downward pressure on inflation.  \par \par \uc2 Schroeder and French Prime Minister Jean-Pierre Raffarin also criticised euro strength this week and called on the ECB to cut rates.  \par \par \uc2 But ECB council member Nicholas Garganas poured cold water on the speculation in a newspaper interview on Friday. He told the Financial Times a strong euro was not stifling the euro zone economy and advised "staying cool" on the exchange rate issue.  \par \par \uc2 "There is always a slight difference between politicians and a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But the question is how long the ECB can justify to hold off cutting interest rates when inflation is moving below actual target," said Niels Christensen, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Societe Generale.  \par \par \uc2 By 1040 GMT the dollar had risen to $1.2374 per euro, up half a percent from late New York levels.  \par \par \uc2 A flash estimate for euro zone inflation, due at 1100 GMT, will attract more attention than usual. The index is forecast at 1.7 percent on the year in February, below the ECB's 2.0 percent target ceiling.  \par \par \uc2 "I'm not sure how deep the euro's adjustment will get, but if you look for euro-negative factors, there are lots of them. The euro zone economy is doing worse than the U.S. and Japan," said Seiya Nakajima, chief economist at Itochu Corp.  \par \par \uc2 The euro also lost ground to the yen, dipping one percent to 134.89 yen. Sterling also lost more than one percent against the yen to 201.51.  \par \par \uc2 JAPAN LESS AGGRESSIVE?  \par \par \uc2 A raft of U.S. data, including fourth-quarter growth and consumer sentiment, is also keenly awaited for clues about the U.S. economy and interest rate outlook.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. gross domestic product data for the fourth quarter is due at 1330 GMT and the University of Michigan consumer sentiment survey is due at 1445 GMT. The Chicago Purchasing Managers' Index is due at 1500 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 "Even if we have weak data, it might be difficult to damage the dollar given the dollar's current momentum," Christensen said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was at 109.01 yen, off this week's three-month high of 109.83. The pair hit three-year lows near 105.15 earlier this month.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Japan sold 3.3420 trillion yen ($30.47 billion) in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in February to stem the yen's rise against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 This compares with a record seven trillion yen Japan spent in January.  \par \par \uc2 "The amount (in February) was a little lower than expected. But with the dollar/yen at current levels, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be less inclined to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily," Christensen said.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier data showed a strong rise in Japan's industrial output in January, underpinning expectations the world's second biggest economy is recovering.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040227e02r0017v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
