\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar firm near recent peaks as euro concerns grow.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Hideyuki Sano  \par \uc2 682 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Februar 2004\par 07:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Feb 27 (Reuters) - The dollar held firm on Friday, sitting near one-month highs against the euro and three-month peaks versus the yen hit the previous day amid speculation that Europe may move to curb the strength of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 European policy makers' growing discontent with the euro's strength, coupled with the dollar's recent muscle, made market players nervous about holding the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , once the darling of the market because of its high yield.  \par \par \uc2 "With \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducting yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a series of European officials starting to verbally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the euro, dollar-short positions may be rolled back," said Mitsuru Sahara, vice president of UFJ Bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealing group.  \par \par \uc2 By 0600 GMT, the euro had eased slightly to $1.2435 from around $1.2445 in late U.S. trade. It was nearly four percent down from life highs hit last week, sitting barely above its trendline from the September low of $1.0760 to the four-week low of $1.2382 hit on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the dollar was little changed around 109.45 yen It was just shy of Thursday's high of 109.84 yen, the highest since December 2, and up four percent from three-year lows hit earlier this month.  \par \par \uc2 Thursday's rise in the dollar was partly driven by speculation that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) may cut interest rates next week after German Chancellor Gerhard Schroeder on Wednesday urged the bank to do so to help exporters.  \par \par \uc2 His comments were echoed by French Prime Minister Jean-Pierre Raffarin, who said on Thursday he shared Schroeder's view on European interest rates and that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates were not in line with economic reality.  \par \par \uc2 While many in the market doubted that ECB easing or \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was imminent, they expected more verbal jawboning from European policy makers, which could cap the euro.  \par \par \uc2 "The question is, are there enough reasons to sell the dollar even in the face of complaints from European and Japanese policy makers," said Fumihiko Kawano, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Nomura Securities.  \par \par \uc2 "The increase in the U.S. current account deficit is slowing down and it is well possible it has stopped ballooning after the dollar's fall in recent months. I think the dollar has hit a bottom."  \par \par \uc2 DOLLAR RISE WON'T LAST?  \par \par \uc2 The dollar has also been helped by speculation that the U.S. Federal Reserve may tighten policy sooner than expected if the sluggish U.S. labour market finally picks up.  \par \par \uc2 But others were less optimistic about the dollar versus the yen, pointing to the Japanese recovery.  \par \par \uc2 A string of Japanese economic data landed on Friday mostly in line with expectations, confirming the recovery is on track.  \par \par \uc2 Industrial output rose 3.4 percent in January from a month earlier, beating market forecasts for a rise of 2.8 percent.  \par \par \uc2 "Given the current state of the Japanese economy, capital outflow from Japan is unlikely," said Seiya Nakajima, chief economist at Itochu Corp.  \par \par \uc2 "That leads me to conclude the dollar's current rise is a technical adjustment."  \par \par \uc2 Still, Japanese authorities were likely to continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the yen's rise and protect \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's exports - seen key to recovery.  \par \par \uc2 "We still are not going to have any real material to get the BOJ (Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) to stop \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market anytime soon," said Naomi Fink, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at BNP Paribas.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will unveil the amount of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in February at 1000 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 "If the data shows \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily again in February after selling a record seven trillion yen (in January), yen-buyers will become discouraged," said Sahara of UFJ.  \par \par \uc2 Later in the day, U.S. gross domestic product data for the fourth quarter is slated to arrive at 1330 GMT and the University of Michigan consumer sentiment survey is due at 1445 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 In addition, the market is keeping an eye on what else Schroeder will say when he meets U.S. President George W. Bush on Friday.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040227e02r000mi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
