\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar keeps gains and is poised to rise further.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Hideyuki Sano   \par \uc2 654 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Februar 2004\par 07:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Feb 27 (Reuters) - The dollar held firm on Friday, sitting near one-month highs against the euro and three-month peaks versus the yen hit the previous day amid speculation that Europe may move to curb the strength of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .    \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been conducting yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a series of European officials started verbally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the euro," said Mitsuru Sahara, vice president of UFJ Bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealing group.    \par \par \uc2  At 0225 GMT, the euro traded around $1.2445 , flat on the day, but nearly four percent down from life highs hit last week. It fell to a four-week low of $1.2382 on Thursday.    \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the dollar was also little changed at 109.50 yen . It was just shy of Thursday's high of 109.84 yen, the highest since December 2, and up four percent from three-year lows hit earlier this month.    \par \par \uc2  Thursday's rise in the dollar was partly driven by speculation that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) may cut interest rates next week after German Chancellor Gerhard Schroeder on Wednesday urged the bank to do so to help exporters.    \par \par \uc2  His comments were echoed by French Prime Minister Jean-Pierre Raffarin, who said on Thursday he shared Schroeder's view on European interest rates and that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates were not in line with economic reality.    \par \par \uc2  While many in the market doubted that ECB easing or \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was imminent, they expected more verbal jawboning from European policy makers, which could cap the euro.    \par \par \uc2  "Central banks won't act if there is outside pressure on them to do something," said Seiya Nakajima, chief economist at Itochu Corp.    \par \par \uc2  "I'm not sure how deep the euro's adjustment will get, but if you look for euro-negative factors, there are lots of them. The euro zone economy is doing worse than the U.S. and Japan," he added.    \par \par \uc2  DOLLAR RISE WON'T LAST?    \par \par \uc2  The dollar has also been helped by speculation that the U.S. Federal Reserve may tighten policy sooner than expected if the sluggish U.S. labour market finally picks up.    \par \par \uc2  UFJ's Sahara said: "The dollar is poised to rise above 110 yen in overseas trade today, and there is more room for it to rise to the 113 yen level, which was hit after the Group of Seven meeting in September."    \par \par \uc2  But others were less optimistic about the dollar versus the yen, pointing to the Japanese recovery.    \par \par \uc2  A string of Japanese economic data released on Friday mostly came in line with expectations, confirming the recovery is on track.    \par \par \uc2  Industrial output rose 3.4 percent in January from a month earlier, beating market forecasts for a rise of 2.8 percent.    \par \par \uc2  "Given the current state of the Japanese economy, capital outflow from Japan is unlikely," said Itochu's Nakajima.    \par \par \uc2  "That leads me to conclude the dollar's current rise is a technical adjustment."    \par \par \uc2  Still, Japanese authorities were likely to continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the yen's rise and protect \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's exports - seen key to recovery.    \par \par \uc2  "We still are not going to have any real material to get the BOJ (Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) to stop \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market anytime soon," said Naomi Fink, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at BNP Paribas.    \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will unveil the amount of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in February at 1000 GMT.    \par \par \uc2  "If the data shows \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily again in February after selling a record seven trillion yen (in January), yen-buyers will become discouraged," said Sahara of UFJ.    \par \par \uc2  Later in the day, U.S. gross domestic product data for the fourth quarter is slated to land at 1330 GMT and the University of Michigan consumer sentiment survey is due at 1445 GMT.    \par \par \uc2  In addition, the market is keeping an eye on what more Schroeder will say when he meets U.S. President George W. Bush on Friday.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040227e02r000kv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
