\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  MOF Sold Y3.342 Trillion In Feb  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 322 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Februar 2004\par 11:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government sold Y3.342 trillion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in February to fight the yen's rise, \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed Friday.  \par \par \uc2 February's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which followed record sales of Y7.155 trillion in January, came as the yen surged to a three-and-a-half year high against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese officials fear a strong yen could derail the nation's economic recovery by hurting exports and exacerbating deflation through lower import prices.  \par \par \uc2 February's yen selling brings the total spent since the start of 2003 to a stunning Y30.554 trillion.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar sank to Y105.16 on Feb. 11, its lowest level since June 2000, before rebounding toward the end of the month thanks in large part to Japan's persistent yen sales.  \par \par \uc2 At 1027 GMT, the dollar was changing hands around Y109.02.  \par \par \uc2 February's data don't show which \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought, but quarterly breakdowns for 2003 show virtually all \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  targeted dollars.  \par \par \uc2 The data covers transactions settled during the month, or \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  carried out between Jan. 29 and Feb. 25. \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trades are settled after two business days.  \par \par \uc2 To finance the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the ministry sold Y4.986 trillion of its U.S. Treasury holdings to the Bank of Japan under a repo agreement, the data also showed.  \par \par \uc2 The arrangement with the BOJ has allowed the ministry to keep selling yen despite running up against its cumulative Y79-trillion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funding limit earlier this year.  \par \par \uc2 That limit was upped earlier this month by Y21 trillion to Y100 trillion through an extra budget for the current fiscal year ending in March. The ministry is seeking a further Y40-trillion rise through the budget for next fiscal year to March 2005.  \par \par \uc2 -By Jonathan Soble, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; jonathan.soble@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Kirsty Mackenzie [ 27-02-04 1030GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040227e02r000ii\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
