\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Buba's Stark says limited export impact from euro.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Victoria Thieberger  \par \uc2 524 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Februar 2004\par 03:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Feb 25 (Reuters) - The vice-president of Germany's Bundesbank \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Juergen Stark said on Wednesday the strong euro had a limited impact on euro zone exports, even as European politicians complained more loudly about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dramatic rise.   \par \par \uc2  "The favorable impact of world trade and world growth dynamics are more important for our exports than the recent decline in price competitiveness caused by the appreciation of the euro," Stark said in a speech before a group of economists in New York.   \par \par \uc2  Stark's comments came only hours after German Chancellor Gerhard Schroeder called upon the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to "most intensively" consider lowering interest rates to counter the euro's strength, an appeal followed by a similar request from the country's head of its BDI industry association.   \par \par \uc2  Stark would not comment directly on Schroeder's remarks but stressed the ECB does not react to short-term events in conducting monetary policy.   \par \par \uc2  Stark signaled he saw no need to move benchmark rates and suggested the ECB was less concerned about the impact of the euro. "In our view, the risks to the outlook of a gradual recovery in the euro area in 2004 are balanced."   \par \par \uc2  But talking to reporters after his speech Stark acknowledged that "in the view of European politicians, there is reason for concern about the excessive movement in the exchange rate."   \par \par \uc2  Stark played down worries about the surprising drop in Germany's Ifo survey of business confidence earlier this week, telling reporters the underlying trend of improvement in the German economy "is intact."   \par \par \uc2  While Stark is not a member of the ECB's policy-setting council, he is seen having intimate knowledge of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's views. Stark often attends the meetings of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governing Council and deputizes for Bundesbank president Ernst Welteke.   \par \par \uc2  MIND THE CURRENT ACCOUNT GAP   \par \par \uc2  Stark said the large U.S. current account deficit remained a key risk to the favorable growth outlook, especially now that capital inflows into the United States were mainly from \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases of Treasuries and no longer from other investors.   \par \par \uc2  "The willingness of overseas investors to hold an ever-growing dollar-denominated portfolio is obviously something which cannot go on forever," Stark said.   \par \par \uc2  Stark also said Asian central banks at some point will have to take a "very careful look" at their holdings of U.S. assets given the possibility of a further decline in the dollar.   \par \par \uc2  Asian central banks, particularly the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , have aggressively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to buy dollars as a way of limiting the export-damaging rise in their own \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  Those purchases are seen as largely financing the U.S. current account gap, which stands at roughly 5 percent of gross domestic product, and helping hold down U.S. interest rates.   \par \par \uc2  The dollar  has had a turbulent few weeks against the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , hitting a record low beyond $1.29 per euro earlier this month and then staging a rebound to a three-week high of $1.2450 per euro on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040226e02q000bc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
