\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: BOJ Mulls Govt Bond Lending, Holds Policy Steady  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Iain McDonald  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 788 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Februar 2004\par 10:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Thursday it may start lending bonds it holds to financial market players, to make trading smoother at a time when the government is faced with the tough task of issuing record amounts of debt.  \par \par \uc2 Bank of Japan Governor Toshihiko Fukui has asked staff to report back soon to the board on a possible lending facility for Japanese government bonds, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.  \par \par \uc2 The system the BOJ is considering is already in place in other advanced bond markets. Under such a system, authorities lend out bonds when players have trouble securing issues they need, and that is threatening to drag down liquidity and lead to problems in pricing.  \par \par \uc2 At a BOJ policy board meeting Thursday, officials said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  "could contribute to enhancing liquidity and maintaining the smooth functioning of government securities markets" by setting up a lending facility, according to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "A similar facility has been adopted by other industrialized nations," Fukui told reporters at a news conference. "So we decided to mull the step preemptively because the bond market remains stable now."  \par \par \uc2 The step would come as Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  plans in the year starting April to issue to the market a record Y117.8 trillion of JGBs, including bonds to refinance maturing debt and Y36.59 trillion of new JGBs to fund the government's gaping fiscal hole.  \par \par \uc2 Both the BOJ and MOF have indicated they will work more closely on debt management policy as the JGB market - already the world's largest government bond market - continues to grow.  \par \par \uc2 The finance ministry has made a series of regulatory changes to the JGB market to help smooth issuance and plans later this year to introduce a primary JGB dealer system.  \par \par \uc2 At Thursday's meeting, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board also voted unanimously to hold its ultra-easy monetary policy steady. That was in line with market expectations since the recent fall and strong Japanese economic data would both argue against the immediate need for further monetary stimulus.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     May Drain Arbitrage Profits \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While the BOJ's announcement it would consider lending JGBs had no impact on JGB prices, dealers and strategists said such a facility would be supportive for the market in the long term.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The plan shows that not only the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but also the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is willing to commit to Japan's debt management," said Yasunari Ueno, chief market economist at Mizuho Securities.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The BOJ already buys Y1.2 trillion of JGBs each month as part of its open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to keep the financial system awash with cash.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fukui said several details about the JGB lending \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  haven't been decided.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Such a system is expected to increase efficiency in Japan's debt market.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It's likely to come in handy, for example, when a securities firm wants to sell a certain issue of JGBs that it doesn't own. Salespeople may feel greater confidence in offering the client a competitive price if they know they could go to the BOJ to borrow the issue for a period of time until the firm could procure the bond in the market.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Lending of JGBs by the BOJ could increase market liquidity, "but probably could take some of the arbitrage profits out of the market for some dealers," said John Richards, Japan strategist at Barclays Capital in Tokyo.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Fukui Welcomes Dollar Recovery \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Separately, Fukui welcomed the dollar's recent recovery against other major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , saying the calmer \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market would help the global economy.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fukui credited an amended statement on exchange rates by the Group of Seven leading industrialized nations with curbing the dollar's sharp decline.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I think an understanding of the G7's intention is sinking into the market with time," he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar fell sharply after the G7 finance officials called for "more flexibility in exchange rates" at their meeting in Dubai last September - a statement that was interpreted as a sign the U.S. wanted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stop \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But the greenback has rebounded since the G7 amended that statement at a meeting earlier this month in Florida, adding a warning against "disorderly" movements in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fukui added that while only time will tell if the dollar's two-year decline against major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has ended, a calmer \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market "would be good for the global economic outlook."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Iain McDonald, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2941; iain.mcdonald@dowjones.com (Hiroshi Inoue, Jonathan Soble and Michiyo Seki contributed to this article).  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Bennett Richardson [ 26-02-04 0940GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040226e02q000gb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
