\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Down As Mkt Ponders  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Report  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Miyako Takebe  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 782 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Februar 2004\par 06:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar edged down against its major counterparts in Asia Thursday as market players pondered the likelihood of dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , not only by the Japanese authorities, but also by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The greenback, which rallied sharply against the euro overnight, continued to find support from a Market News International report the ECB may consider \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  together with the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the euro.  \par \par \uc2 The report, which cited unnamed sources from the ECB, also said the ECB would discuss cutting interest rates at its next policy meeting on March 4. Japanese officials declined to comment on the report or any possibility of joint action.  \par \par \uc2 While not many Tokyo traders believed there would be any immediate ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or an interest rate cut, especially after the dollar's rally overnight, many still felt uneasy chasing the euro higher.  \par \par \uc2 "It's a bit scary buying the euro now," said a trader at a Japanese bank.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the more imminent and tangible threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's authorities kept the dollar afloat against the yen. However it was unable to hold on to the day's high of Y109.19 amid selling by a variety of players to adjust positions, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 One \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader noted that those at Japanese banks often associated with the BOJ have been remarking that authorities appear "dead set" on continuing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , even as the dollar shows signs of recovering.  \par \par \uc2 "Their goal now appears not necessarily to help Japan's exporters, but rather to annihilate short dollar positions which have been behind the dollar's earlier plunge," to three-year lows, the Tokyo trader said.  \par \par \uc2 Comments from Zembei Mizoguchi, Japan's vice finance minister for international affairs, suggested that may be the case. He said Thursday morning that adjustments of short positions were entering a "firm trend," and were helping stabilize the market.  \par \par \uc2 Moreover, Japan's Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said earlier this week that the market appears to be "reassessing" speculative movements to sell the dollar which had been occurring in the wake of the Group of Seven meeting in Dubai in September.  \par \par \uc2 Some traders say that while the MOF is unlikely targeting any specific level, it may not rest until the dollar recovers to around Y115 - which is where it was trading at around the time of the Dubai meeting.  \par \par \uc2 At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y108.83, below Y109.03 late Wednesday in New York, but above Y108.17 late Wednesday in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.2509, higher than $1.2490 late Wednesday in New York. The euro was at $1.2678 in Tokyo Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y136.14, down from Y136.21 in New York late Wednesday. The euro was at Y137.14 in Tokyo late Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.8769, up from $1.8691 in New York but lower than $1.8894 in Tokyo Wednesday. [ 26-02-04 0546GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was unmoved by the BOJ's decision to hold monetary policy steady Wednesday. The no-change verdict was expected given that Japan's economy is still on a mild recovery track and the dollar has rebounded slightly from its lows earlier this year.  \par \par \uc2 But \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  players fear \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's MOF may continue with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and become bolder, given the show of support for Tokyo's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy expressed Wednesday by the head of the International Monetary Fund.  \par \par \uc2 Both Tanigaki and Mizoguchi said that IMF Managing Director Horst Koehler understands and is supportive of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's massive \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the yen's rise.  \par \par \uc2 "We share a common view on this issue," Tanigaki told a parliamentary committee. "To put it a little more strongly, our stance has been heartily accepted" by the IMF.  \par \par \uc2 Koehler told a press conference in Tokyo that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was an effective deflation-fighting tool given the lack of other monetary policy options. He added that he believed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is being used primarily as an adjunct of monetary policy, rather than as a trade weapon, and that it was likely only temporary.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; miyako.takebe@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Alastair Gale  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The chart of late Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates that accompanied Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been replaced with an enhanced \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Subscribers can find this table:  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX [ 26-02-04 0642GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1074  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040226e02q0005j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
